-- title:
--   G Comm Stability Two Raw Scalar
-- statement:
--   **Raw scalar form of the second G-commutativity stability bound.** Let $S$ be a symmetric projective strategy for $(m+1,q,d)$ with normalized state, let $G^x$ be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family for $(m,q,d)$, and let $\zeta$ be an error parameter. Assume the family identity and the `SliceBoundednessInput` with error $\zeta$.
--
--   For fixed $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$, let $T_x$ be the total operator of $G^x$. For a successor point $r$, write $B^r_b$ for the evaluated point-family effect, write $P^r_b$ for the strategy point-measurement effect, and write $P^{(u,x)}_{g(u)}$ for the effect at the appended point. Define the uncollapsed defect
--
--   $$
--   \Delta_2(x)=\mathbb E_{r\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^{m+1})}\mathbb E_{u\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q^m)}\sum_{g,b}\operatorname{ev}_\psi\!\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(G^x_gB^r_b(1-T_x))\,\operatorname{rightTensor}(P^r_bP^{(u,x)}_{g(u)})\right).
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \left|\mathbb E_{x\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathbb{F}_q)}\Delta_2(x)\right|\le\sqrt{\zeta}.
--   $$
--
--   This is the raw post-swap form of the second scalar stability estimate, before its right-register sandwich is packaged.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Commutativity.gCommStabilityTwo_raw_scalar`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Commutativity/GCommStability/Scalar/RawSecond.lean#L635-L674

